<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <PackageId>ResponseResultHandler</PackageId>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <Title>Response Result Handler</Title>
    <Version>16.1.0</Version>
    <Product>ResponseResultHandler</Product>
    <Description>The Result pattern for .NET: an immutable result with an HTTP-mappable status, a title and detail, errors keyed by field and optional data, plus Map, Bind, Ensure and Combine to chain them without exceptions. No dependencies.</Description>
    <PackageIcon>ResultHandlerIcon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageTags>result result-pattern railway-oriented-programming functional error-handling validation</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>v16.1 - Map, Bind, Ensure, Match, OnSuccess, OnFailure (sync and async) and Combine throw ArgumentNullException naming the parameter when given null; async methods throw before returning their task. See CHANGELOG.md.

v16.0 - Breaking (serialization): a serialized result writes "errors" as the field-to-messages map Problem Details use ("" for messages without a field) and no longer writes "fieldErrors". Breaking (API): IOperationResult.Errors is the field-to-messages map ("" for messages without a field), replacing the flat Errors list, FieldErrors, IHasFieldErrors and GetFieldErrors(); the 1xx factories and UseProxy are removed. New: IOperationResult.Location, WithLocation(uri); redirect factories set Location. Versions move together; see CHANGELOG.md.

v15.0 - No changes in this package; ResponseResultHandler.AspNetCore adds an exception handler, async endpoint adapters and a smaller success envelope, and ResponseResultHandler.FluentValidation is new. Versions move together; see CHANGELOG.md.

v14.0.1 - No changes in this package; ResponseResultHandler.AspNetCore fixes MVC validation failures losing "errors". Versions move together.

v14.0 - Breaking: IOperationResult.Code added. New WithCode(code) attaches a machine-readable error code, serialized as "code" and carried through Map/Bind/ToErrorDataResult. Versions move together; see CHANGELOG.md.

v13.3 - No changes in this package; ResponseResultHandler.AspNetCore adds ProducesEnveloped() for OpenAPI. Versions move together.

v13.2 - No changes in this package; ResponseResultHandler.AspNetCore adds ProducesResultProblems() for OpenAPI. Versions move together.

v13.1 - Bind into commands that return no data:

Added:
- Bind/BindAsync overloads whose binder returns a result with no data (IOperationResult, or Task&lt;OperationResult&gt; such as a MediatR command Send), so a data result chains into a command in one expression. Failures keep title, status, detail, errors and field errors. Existing overloads are unchanged.

See CHANGELOG.md for full details.

v13.0 (breaking) - Result facade returns the common base types, plus async overloads for MediatR-style concrete results:

Changed (breaking):
- Every Result facade factory now returns OperationResult (was SuccessResult/ErrorResult) or OperationDataResult&lt;T&gt; (was SuccessDataResult&lt;T&gt;/ErrorDataResult&lt;T&gt;). Success and failure branches share one static type, so `cond ? Result.Success(x) : Result.NotFound&lt;T&gt;(...)` and lambdas returning both compile without casts or explicit type arguments. Runtime types are unchanged.
- Result.Created/Result.Accepted (and their &lt;T&gt; forms) are explicit overload pairs instead of an optional title parameter; existing calls compile unchanged.
- Binary breaking: assemblies compiled against 12.x must be recompiled.

Added:
- MapAsync/BindAsync/MatchAsync/OnSuccessAsync/OnFailureAsync/EnsureAsync overloads for Task&lt;OperationDataResult&lt;T&gt;&gt; and Task&lt;OperationResult&gt; sources (for example a MediatR Send), and BindAsync binders returning Task&lt;OperationDataResult&lt;TOut&gt;&gt;.

Migration: change variables, return types or delegates declared as a concrete subclass (ErrorResult e = Result.Conflict(...), Func&lt;string, ErrorResult&gt;) to OperationResult/OperationDataResult&lt;T&gt; or use var. See CHANGELOG.md for full details.

v12.1 - Per-field validation errors, plus FieldErrors bug fixes:

Added:
- Per-field validation errors: IHasFieldErrors, IResultFailureFactory&lt;TSelf&gt;.Failure(fieldErrors), OperationResult.Failure(fieldErrors) (see README "Per-field validation errors"). Breaking for any external IResultFailureFactory&lt;TSelf&gt; implementer - see CHANGELOG.md.

Fixed:
- Map/Bind/ToErrorDataResult() dropped FieldErrors when re-projecting a failure into a different result type - now preserved, along with the original Errors list.
- Result.Combine(...) dropped FieldErrors when merging failures - field errors from every combined failure are now merged by key.
- Failure(fieldErrors) threw if the dictionary had a null value - that field's messages are skipped instead.
- GetHashCode() was order-sensitive for FieldErrors while Equals() wasn't, so equal-content dictionaries with a different key order could hash differently.
- OperationResult/OperationDataResult&lt;T&gt;'s errors+fieldErrors constructor is now public, so Native AOT source-generated JSON deserializers can call it.

Removed (breaking):
- net7.0 support (EOL) - net8.0/net9.0/net10.0 only; upgrade your target framework before taking this version.

See CHANGELOG.md for full details.

v12 (breaking): Removed all members previously marked [Obsolete] — StatusMessage, StatusCode, ResultData, and every HttpStatusCode-based constructor across OperationResult/OperationDataResult/SuccessResult/SuccessDataResult/ErrorResult/ErrorDataResult. Use Title/Status/Data and the ResultStatus-based constructors instead (see README "Migrating to v12"). Also includes the previously-unreleased v11.1 additions: Result.Combine, Ensure/EnsureAsync guard clauses, and Task-aware async composition helpers (MatchAsync/OnSuccessAsync/OnFailureAsync/MapAsync/BindAsync). See CHANGELOG.md for details.</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="ResultHandlerIcon.png">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="ResultHandler.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Build.Tasks.Git" Version="10.0.403">
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.PublicApiAnalyzers" Version="5.6.0">
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
    </PackageReference>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Update="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="10.0.403" />
    <PackageReference Update="SonarAnalyzer.CSharp" Version="10.35.0.4138" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
